From 109d417cd6184a18b7bb359941f532d1ef5e5e0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Stosse <1315-Harvester57@users.noreply.git.frama-c.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 08:48:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [wp] read hexadecimal floating-point literals and the f32/f64
 suffixes

Cfloat.parse_literal only read decimal digits, and accepted any text
ending with f, l or d after them. As a result:

- a hexadecimal literal without suffix, such as 0x1.8p1 or DBL_MAX
  from Frama-C's <float.h>, was rejected with "Unexpected constant
  literal": in a contract the term was replaced by an unknown value (a
  hypothesis using it was lost), and in a lemma WP stopped;
- with -wp-model +real, a suffixed one such as 0x1.8p1f was read as 0,
  without any message: "0x1.8p1f == 0.0" was proved by Qed;
- the f32 and f64 suffixes, which the kernel accepts since 33.0, were
  rejected, as in 1.5f32.

The suffix is now removed with Floating_point.extract_suffix, the rest
must be read entirely, and a hexadecimal literal (including an optional
leading sign, matching re_mantissa for literals emitted by
Logic_const.treal under -float-print hex) is converted to its exact
rational value. In the Float model a suffixed literal still denotes the
value rounded by the kernel, as before.

New test: wp_acsl/float_literals.i, in both models and with
-float-print hex.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
